   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "זֶה הַכְּלָל: כֹּל שֶׁהוּא לְדַעַת — אָסוּר. לְאֵיתוֹיֵי מַאי? לְאֵיתוֹיֵי גְּרָמָא.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches that «this» is «the principle:» In the case of «any» blemish «that is» caused «with» his «intent,» the animal’s slaughter is «prohibited.» The Gemara explains: «What» does this principle serve «to add?» It serves «to add an indirect» action, i.e., a blemish caused in this manner is also considered an intentional act and the animal may not be slaughtered on its account."
  }
